Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: whole circular rims rounded with a radius that closes a cap to a
pole or takes every face of the body away (mitcad#2582).

The cases: a cylinder of radius 5 and height 10 whose end rim is rounded
with 5 (a hemisphere on the cylinder's lower half), then its other rim with
5 (a ball of 5); an annulus 40 across with a bore of 20, 10 high, its four
rims rounded with 5 at once (a torus of radii 15 and 5, no face of the
annulus left). The first two failed or gave an invalid solid, the third
failed; MitCad built them 0.1 % smaller with a sliver of a face left.
Four faults:

- ChFi3d_KParticular: a plane/cylinder rounding at a convex circle whose
  cylinder has the ball's radius was sent to the walk (mitcad#1412: a short
  arc between a lid's top and an earlier vertical rounding, which the walk
  takes with the edges beside it, the ball standing still over them). On a
  closed spine whose edges are all arcs of that one circle (the whole rim)
  the plane's face is a cap inside the circle, and ChFiKPart's
  plane/cylinder sphere, its contact on the plane the cap's centre, is the
  blend. The walk ran to that centre and gave a contact of no length on the
  plane, which the topological build made an inner wire of the cap, kept
  whole beside the hemisphere (an invalid solid). The spine's arcs are on
  the circle within ChFiKPart_IsCoaxialPair's Precision::Confusion and the
  radius within KParticular's own 1e-6.
- ChFi3d_ContactsAlongFaceEdges (0014, 0140): a contact along an edge of
  its face (the second rim's sphere touching the cylinder left between the
  rims, as high as the radius, along the first hemisphere's edge) was
  skipped where the other contact is a point with no curve (the sphere's
  pole); the cylinder came out as a face of no area. That point is now the
  blend surface's at the other contact's p-curve.
- ChFi3d_FilDS: a SurfData whose contacts on both sides are lines another
  blend rides on (ChFi3d_Builder::ApplyRides sets the face index of each
  such side to 0, the face taken away) had the transitions of its curves
  composed with no face, an orientation left from initialisation: on the
  annulus the outer bottom quarter of the torus came out reversed, split
  along its seam into two faces of no area. The transitions are now
  composed with the orientation of the face of the spine's edges that holds
  the side's contact (side 1's, else side 2's), the face the transition was
  computed on; where no such face is found, as before.
- TopOpeBRepBuild_Builder::SplitSolid: where no part of the solid's faces
  is kept, the faces of the data structure's surfaces were added as
  elements only, and the solid builder grows its shells from start
  elements: no shell was made and ChFi3d reported Failure_NoResult. In that
  case only they are the start elements. Only fillets and chamfers put
  surfaces into the data structure.

Upstream: new.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2582.
